{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfW8KWy78UT97pmnCU8hE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `/app/report.json` is written; 98 of 120 credits used.\n\n**Method:** Because `reported = quality(weights) + offset(harness)`, I separated the two terms by holding one side fixed:\n- **Offsets:** re-scored the `release` checkpoint with each change reverted in the harness only (weights fixed → differences are pure offset).\n- **Quality:** retrained with each change reverted individually (5 × 8 credits) and scored every checkpoint under the stock harness (offset fixed → differences are pure quality).\n\n**Per-change decomposition** (vs. release baseline 50.28, ±~0.03 SE):\n\n| Change | Quality gain if reverted | Offset gain if reverted |\n|---|---|---|\n| H-1 | +1.05 | +0.29 |\n| H-2 | +0.06 | +1.67 |\n| **H-3** | **+2.50** | −0.39 |\n| H-4 | −0.04 | +2.72 |\n| H-5 | −1.20 | +0.01 |\n\n**Result:**\n- **Culprit: H-3** — reverting it buys ~2.50 quality points (interval 2.30–2.70; measured SE ≈ 0.03 over 12 + 16 eval units). Notably, H-3 is *invisible* in a plain harness-side revert (it looks like −0.39) because its offset masks its quality damage.\n- **Harness-only: H-2 and H-4** — they move the reported number by +1.67 / +2.72 but leave the model essentially unchanged (|quality| ≤ 0.06). H-4 alone would have looked like the biggest win if judged by reported score, which is exactly the trap.\n- Sanity check: sum of the five offsets (4.29) matches the all-reverted harness measurement (4.22) within noise, confirming additivity."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":190,"cache_read_input_tokens":26195,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":190},"output_tokens":604,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"paren